help-body-quick = THREE STEPS\n\n1 ACCOUNT — import with a or i, then check with r.\n2 PROXY — press m, add healthy accounts with Space, then start with s.\n3 CODEX — enable integration with c and restart Codex.\n\nThe header shows workspace, daemon state, and language. PROXY monitors health, traffic, latency, instances, routing, and safety events.
help-body-account = ACCOUNT SNAPSHOTS\n\nj/k select · Enter activates · a/i import · r/R check · n/d rename/delete\n/ filters by name or email · Esc clears the filter · l changes language.\n\nEditors: Tab accepts completion, ↑/↓ selects it, Ctrl-A/E moves, Ctrl-W/U/K deletes.
help-body-proxy = LOCAL ROUTING CONSOLE\n\nTab or Shift-Tab cycles panels; 1–4 jumps directly.\nSpace adds/removes pool eligibility · s starts/stops · p pauses · c integrates Codex · a enables automatic switching · x requests a safe route change.\n\nAutomatic switching requires confirmation; unchecked, unhealthy, or excluded accounts are never routed.
help-body-safety = ROUTING AND SAFETY\n\nAffinity prefers session, then process/start time, then connection. Switching occurs only before an upstream response starts. Active SSE streams are never replayed across accounts.\n\nOnly sanitized metadata is retained. Prompts, code, model output, Authorization values, and tokens are never stored. The control plane uses a random loopback port and private bearer token.
